{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130447-need-help-for-my-new-chronicle-with-a-few-revenant-questions","id":1130447,"title":"Need help for my new chronicle (with a few revenant questions)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-17T13:43:07-07:00","id":1130447,"title":"Need help for my new chronicle (with a few revenant questions)","content":"I am starting a new chronicle soon that will be set in Venice in 1204-1205, a little bit after the sack of constantinople. I have put in place the setting and the npcs but i am having some second thought on how i planned the early phase of the chronicle.<br /> <br /> The players will start as mortals grouped together to see about stealing and/or smuggling some treasures from the sack of constantinople. I'm doing it that way because i feel it provides an easy way for the player to form a group while offering a good enough variety on character backgrounds.<br /> One of the treasures will be a big crate (about as big as a coffin wink wink) that will be more secured than the other.<br /> So instead of treasures out will come a low humanity powerful vampire that kill and drinks the PCs. <br /> Next night the players wake up as revenants and the game officially start. Now i know that for 4-5 people to come back as revenant back to back is unlikely but i think i'll introduce that as a relevant mystery to solve for the players.<br /> The beginning will be about coming to terms with what they've become and that survival is easier as a group. After a while, i've planned for the player to gain the opportunity to have their character join a clan.<br /> <br /> So my questions are thus:<br /> <br /> 1. Is surviving as a revenant too punishing for players? I don't know how difficult being a revenant is. If its very punishing then i will offer the opportunity to join a clan much earlier than i've planned.<br /> <br /> 2. What are the ways to leave revenantdom and join a clan? I mean, i know you can diablerise to become a vampire of the clan or a vampire can expand a willpower dot to sort of post-embrace you into the clan. But i admit that i am drawing a blank on scenarios to allow those things to happen.<br /> Ideally i'd like for the player to take a way to become full kindred instead of being offered the option.<br /> <br /> 3. The game starts officially when they become revenant, but in the books it assumes that you've been a vampire for about a year. So what changes on the character sheet does that entails (like with merits and stuff)? I've been thinking on actually starting the players at humanity 10 and have it plummet to 7 then stabilize until they join a clan. <br /> <br /> Thank you for your help<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T03:58:16-07:00","id":1130762,"title":"","content":"Salut, Ma\u00eetre Corbeau sur ton arbre perch\u00e9,<br /> <br /> I like the question because in the second part of the prologue of my current chronicle has had my PCs turned into revenants. Let's be honest here: it's brutal as sh*t ! Five game years later, their characters still deal with the consequences of what they did as revenant. It's hard but very interesting as it is a perfect extreme introduction to what it means to be a bloodthirsty monster. However, if you play it with the rules as they are, I don't think it can be sustainable on the long term. I would play it as a phase of your chronicle. My PCs had to understand what was happening to them and find the one who had unwillingly turned them so she could make them true vampires. It's a nice plot hook, but it can't really last.<br /> <br /> Now, if they are just recently turned vampires, it's really your choice what powers you give them. Personally, when they turned revenant, I gave them one dot of discipline. When they turned true vampires, I believe I gave them one other dot to spend. It's purely a personal choice though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12610-lestat","name":"Lestat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12610_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T10:10:04-07:00","id":1130875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lestat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130447-need-help-for-my-new-chronicle-with-a-few-revenant-questions?p=1130762#post1130762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Salut, Ma\u00eetre Corbeau sur ton arbre perch\u00e9,<br /> <br /> I like the question because in the second part of the prologue of my current chronicle has had my PCs turned into revenants. Let's be honest here: it's brutal as sh*t ! Five game years later, their characters still deal with the consequences of what they did as revenant. It's hard but very interesting as it is a perfect extreme introduction to what it means to be a bloodthirsty monster. However, if you play it with the rules as they are, I don't think it can be sustainable on the long term. I would play it as a phase of your chronicle. My PCs had to understand what was happening to them and find the one who had unwillingly turned them so she could make them true vampires. It's a nice plot hook, but it can't really last..</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, i was afraid of that. I'm thinking of softening it up a bit by ruling that they only lose their blood point up to how many they are sleeping. So with 4 players they would wake up with 4 blood point every night. <br /> But regardless, i'll try not to have them stay too long in that state, maybe 3 session max. What i'll do is i'll have the kindred of the city find them and force them to find the vampire that made them.<br /> <br /> So i've thought of 3 scenarios for them to leave the revenant state depending on what the players want.<br /> <br /> 1. They impress the kindred of the city enough that they are offered an opportunity to be uplifted.<br /> <br /> 2. They do not impress the kindred of the city that subsequently try to get rid of them as they are no longer useful. In the process the PCs escape and find/overpower 4 weak kindred and diablerise them.<br /> <br /> 3. They find their maker that offers them to become neglatu (i'll have to reread the rules concerning them). The players each make their own nests of revenant (i'll probably have it be a merit like allies or something) but still work together against the kindred of the city.<br /> <br /> at the start i'll probably allow them to take a point from the physical discipline. Then when they become part of a clan they gain a dot of that clans discipline. With the last dot given freely after a few other games (perhaps when joining a covenant or other similar milestone).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T00:57:26-07:00","id":1131157,"title":"","content":"I'll offer another suggestion which is not necessarily better but it gives you anothet choice.<br /> <br /> Overpowering four kindred to diablerize them may be a bit much. They can find one and overpower him. Then one player diablerize him, gets uplifted then uplifts another player who then does the same and so on. Sure it hurts their humanity but it is quite thematic. My players did that except they bargained to have one of them uplifted instead of diablerizing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12610-lestat","name":"Lestat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12610_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T10:14:56-07:00","id":1132266,"title":"","content":"They need to learn how to survive fast, I would recommend someone explaining what they are on night one and maybe serving as a mentor as needed but either weak themselves or with their own interests that they will prioritise. For example a Dragon who's willing to help his test subjects out but his experiments come at a risk to the participants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T06:09:29-07:00","id":1132985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130447-need-help-for-my-new-chronicle-with-a-few-revenant-questions?p=1132266#post1132266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They need to learn how to survive fast, I would recommend someone explaining what they are on night one and maybe serving as a mentor as needed but either weak themselves or with their own interests that they will prioritise. For example a Dragon who's willing to help his test subjects out but his experiments come at a risk to the participants.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Ghoul, or former Ghoul might also give you that blend of knowledge and ignorance mixed with desperation.<br /> <br /> For the frankly harsh Feeding requirements, you could also phase them in. They only lose 1 Vitae a night the first week, then 2 the next week, etc. Build a sense of urgency.<br /> <br /> Or let them uncover ways (or Merits) that let them retain more Vitae during their sleeps. Makes acquiring whatever that is a priority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T14:51:40-07:00","id":1133174,"title":"","content":"New Mystery Cult: The Revernts For Self Preservation.<br /> First dot. The membership insist you take steps to not to screw up, the ST will assign you a skill specialisation that the cult believes will keep you safe, this is usually to mitigate a weakness.<br /> Second dot. The cult will let you at their supply of rats, gain the herd merit at the same level you have in this merit.<br /> Third dot. Someone's taken a liking to you, gain a two dot mentor.<br /> Fourth dot. You know who's worth listening to, gain a three dot library in a subject you can justify representing your ability to make the most of your fellow cult members.<br /> Fifth dot. Enough already, someone will embrace/uplift you when there's an opening, when they do trade this merit in under sanctity of merits as standard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T09:28:41-07:00","id":1133417,"title":"","content":"Oof apologies for silence, i've had a busy few days.<br /> <br /> So we had the session 0 where i set up the setting and we discuss on themes and make the characters. Now they are okay with starting as revenant as a way to experience to worst of being vampires (although it took a little convincing for some players) but they are adamant about joining a clan. Too bad because i love the idea of a revenant cult/covenant that Live Bait made.<br /> <br /> As for the mentor idea. It is genius and i'm definitely going with it. But the idea i had is a bit unorthodox i think and i want your opinions on if its feasible. What if the players soon after theyre transformation are found by a strix that is forcibly bound inside a rat's corpse? The idea here is that the character have access to a very dangerous source of information but that is still manageable for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T12:16:17-07:00","id":1133491,"title":"","content":"What about using a <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Neglatu\" target=\"_blank\">Neglatu</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T08:57:41-07:00","id":1133814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130447-need-help-for-my-new-chronicle-with-a-few-revenant-questions?p=1133417#post1133417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Too bad because i love the idea of a revenant cult/covenant that Live Bait made.</div> </div> </div> </div>Happy to help, it's been in my head for a while now and I'm always happy when ideas find a good home. I will say that there's no reason it can't still be used if you want as Santity of Merits would kick in when they get their clan so all it needs is a population of Revrents organised enough to keep a rat farm. I also must say that I love the rat Strix (whom I may start calling Ratix).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}